<urn:atm:triage:finding/S12-QA1-006>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "S12-QA1-006" ;
  triage:title "Unconditional condvar wait inside bounded_shutdown_step_returns_after_deadline test closure (RSH-006)" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health.rs:880: The bounded_shutdown_step_returns_after_deadline test uses wake.wait(released) (unconditional Condvar::wait) inside the step closure rather than a timed wait. If notify_all fires before the thread is scheduled, the wait blocks indefinitely — the only safety net is the drain_shutdown_finalizer_threads_for_test() finalizer, which itself has a fixed timeout. This is a test design gap consistent with INTG-FTQ-002/003 class (wall-clock/timing sensitivity). Fix: replace wake.wait(released) with wake.wait_timeout(released, Duration::from_secs(5)) and assert !timed_out, consistent with the pattern used in reconcile_runtime tests exercising the same scenario." ;
  triage:category "FTQ" ;
  triage:severity "minor" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-S" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
